{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470507-a-trinity-setting-with-novas-psions-and-talents","id":1470507,"title":"A Trinity Setting with Novas, Psions, and Talents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-14T23:07:05-08:00","id":1470507,"title":"A Trinity Setting with Novas, Psions, and Talents?","content":"I wonder if we'll ever get a setting with all three types in play, not as hostile factions, but as allies. Because it's been mentioned in numerous places that on of humanity's big special &quot;hat&quot; is the fact that alone of all the groups out there--mankind can simultaneously develop nova, psi, and talented individuals--and yet at least for now, each setting focuses on one single type, with the others more or less sidelined. <br /> <br /> So do you think there will ever be a published setting with all the groups available as protagonists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T23:26:19-08:00","id":1470508,"title":"","content":"If such a setting does get published - I don't think it's going to come from Onyx Path. They've already got MANY irons in the fire, not many devs/testers/editors to work with, and a backlog of things they've already committed to publishing. That said, I can easily imagine a third-party doing so through their DriveThru community program (can't recall the name, but a few minor releases have come out using it already).<br /> <br /> Personally, I ignore the setting material and use the rules to play in my own worlds. I have one where it's Talents &amp; Psions in a space opera setting very reminiscent of Mass Effect. I have another I'm playing with my sons which is basically The Boys (comic, not TV series) with a very basic make-over that allows Aberrants &amp; Talents to work side-by-side. The Aberrants start at 75pt's of XP instead of 150pts in character generation to give the group a relatively level starting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T23:27:03-08:00","id":1470509,"title":"","content":"Maybe the one that is set in the far future past Aeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T23:36:25-08:00","id":1470510,"title":"","content":"If Aegis, the Greek Mythology setting, ever gets greenlit, it might be a possibility there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T23:59:03-08:00","id":1470511,"title":"","content":"Technically Adventure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T02:02:33-08:00","id":1470515,"title":"","content":"Yes, Adventure! explicitly covers all three types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T02:16:38-08:00","id":1470516,"title":"","content":"Technically speaking, shouldn't Aeon count too? Especially in the later phases, there are more than a few occasions when Psions, Novas and Talents work together - and AFTER the second Aberrant War, diplomatic relations with Eden can be expected and humanity will most likely get used to the idea that there are still uncorrupted Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T04:32:12-08:00","id":1470522,"title":"","content":"A far future space opera setting seems like the best bet. Something rather Baroque set about as far into the future as King Narmer of Egypt is behind us. White Wolf play tested a game like that back in the nineties. It never got beyond the playtest stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T12:00:11-08:00","id":1470539,"title":"","content":"I've been working on this for some time now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> When it's done, I'll put at Storypath Nexus. I was waiting for a good moment to show you, and, maybe that's now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (below is my &quot;teaser&quot; that will be in the back cover of the book) <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">There was a time\u2026 when Flux wielders thought their uncanny abilities were simply luck or great skill.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when Novas thought it was impossible to avoid the corruption of their bodies and minds.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when humankind hadn\u2019t yet achieved their full and unshackled Psionic potential.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when aliens tried to smother the human power \u2013 and human life \u2013 from the cosmos.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when Earth still existed.<br /> <br /> We are beyond that time now.<br /> <br /> <b>Trinity Continuum: Beyond</b>\u2122 is a <i>Storypath Nexus</i> product for those who wish to play in a new age of knowledge, a distant future in which humankind finally understands and harnesses the three most powerful sources of power in the universe: Flux, Quantum, and Psi \u2013 but also lost Earth, long, long ago.</span><br /> </div> <div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><i>created by Frank Malcher</i></span> <hr /></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T14:01:31-08:00","id":1470550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470507-a-trinity-setting-with-novas-psions-and-talents?p=1470516#post1470516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically speaking, shouldn't Aeon count too? Especially in the later phases, there are more than a few occasions when Psions, Novas and Talents work together - and AFTER the second Aberrant War, diplomatic relations with Eden can be expected and humanity will most likely get used to the idea that there are still uncorrupted Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if you count Aeon then really any era would count. Psiad's are pretty much always a possible player character option, and you'd even have the odd Nova show up occasionally. Each era is more about a character type being ascendent, not about the other character types not being available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T17:41:11-08:00","id":1470564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470507-a-trinity-setting-with-novas-psions-and-talents?p=1470539#post1470539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been working on this for some time now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> When it's done, I'll put at Storypath Nexus. I was waiting for a good moment to show you, and, maybe that's now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (below is my &quot;teaser&quot; that will be in the back cover of the book) <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">There was a time\u2026 when Flux wielders thought their uncanny abilities were simply luck or great skill.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when Novas thought it was impossible to avoid the corruption of their bodies and minds.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when humankind hadn\u2019t yet achieved their full and unshackled Psionic potential.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when aliens tried to smother the human power \u2013 and human life \u2013 from the cosmos.<br /> <br /> There was a time\u2026 when Earth still existed.<br /> <br /> We are beyond that time now.<br /> <br /> <b>Trinity Continuum: Beyond</b>\u2122 is a <i>Storypath Nexus</i> product for those who wish to play in a new age of knowledge, a distant future in which humankind finally understands and harnesses the three most powerful sources of power in the universe: Flux, Quantum, and Psi \u2013 but also lost Earth, long, long ago.</span><br /> </div><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><i>created by Frank Malcher</i></span> <hr /></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I don't think you'll be able to put that product out. One of the &quot;rules&quot; of Storypath for Aeon is &quot;no new time settings.&quot; You can put products out for Aeon and Aberrant (and eventually Adventure, Assassins and Anima) but they don't want you putting out your own time settings because you might step on eventual official products.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T19:14:49-08:00","id":1470576,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a time travel setting that links the three would violate the conditions. Granted, you'd have to take steps to keep your time travelers hidden; perhaps something like the Shadow in TC:Assassins? But motivated by a need to not disrupt the timeline. (If I were waiting it, I'd take a lot of inspiration from <i>Continuum: Adventuring in the Yet</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:06:26-08:00","id":1470616,"title":"","content":"Given that bizarre wonder machines and portals to other realities are a thing in the background of each setting, why not a have something of that type teleport people from Earth to another habitable world in another galaxy. If the device was built as a escape path during the Aberrant Wars but blew up in it's creator's face creating a crack in timespace going back centuries, then you could justify all kinds of cultures and peoples living there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}